# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF
# in the working tree. Two checks here compare a file on disk against freshly
# generated, always-LF output -- the pin drift test, and the CI drift job that
# regenerates the header and bindings -- so a CRLF checkout fails them even
# when nothing has actually drifted. hegel-rust pins its generated header for
# the same reason.
#
# Dart sources are LF everywhere regardless, so normalize the whole tree.
* text=auto eol=lf
